      "sentence_id": 4,
      "text": "01. The petitioner is aggrieved of final assessment report dated 12.04.2023 issued by the Deputy Commissioner, Jammu whereby an amount of Rs. 1,90,00,000/- has been assessed to be full and final compensation amount admissible to the concerned land owners with respect to the land which finds mention in the apportionment statement in the final assessment report.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 487,
      "end": 849,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "12.04.2023",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 552,
          "end": 562
        },
        {
          "text": "Jammu",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 598,
          "end": 603
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "text": "Petitioner-Vinod Kumar's name figures as the owner as well as the tenant.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 850,
      "end": 923,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Vinod Kumar",
          "label": "PETITIONER",
          "start": 861,
          "end": 872
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 6,
      "text": "02. Although, the final assessment report being impugned herein is still to be carried forward towards logical end under the Requisition and Acquisition of Remote Property Act, 1968 which would afford a legal remedy to the petitioner as being an aggrieved land owner who is sought to be paid less compensation than the expected one.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 925,
      "end": 1257,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Requisition and Acquisition of Remote Property Act, 1968",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1050,
          "end": 1106
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "03. Since the co-ordinate Bench has already taken notice of the matter at the instance of the similarly aggrieved land owners figuring in the same very assessment report and, as such, issue notice to the respondents.",
